<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sri Lankan Tamils</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ceylon Tamils, Eelam Tamils</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sri Lankan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tamils">Tamils</a> are the Tamil-speaking people native to northern and eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaffna">Jaffna</a> as their cultural centre. Mostly <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a>, with a Christian minority, they formed the Jaffna kingdom in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>. Tensions with the Sinhalese-dominated state after independence led to the civil war of 1983 to 2009, which drove many into a worldwide diaspora.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sri-lankan-tamils.jpg" alt="Sri Lankan Tamils" width="249" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ceylon_Tamil_girl_1910.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
